## Where code goes

| Concern | Location |
|---|---|
| Settings, URLs, ASGI, Celery config | `backend/config/` |
| **Anything that touches two apps at once** | `backend/core/` — the only place allowed to |
| Signal receivers wiring app A's event to app B | `backend/core/signals.py` |
| Multi-app orchestration (checkout, onboarding) | `backend/core/services/` |
| Overrides/subclasses of an app's views | `backend/core/views/` |
| Host-only shared helpers | `backend/tools/` — never imported by an app package |
| Tests for all of the above | `backend/core/tests/` |
| Template overrides | `backend/templates/<app_module>/…` (mirror the app's path) |
| Cross-app UI composition | `frontend/app/` |

## Non-negotiables

- Every view has a `throttle_scope`, and the scope exists in `DEFAULT_THROTTLE_RATES`.
- Every view has a `drf-spectacular` `@extend_schema` with the right `tags`.
- Every model field used for filtering/ordering is indexed; every queryset uses
  `select_related`/`prefetch_related`.
- Signal receivers accept `**kwargs`, never raise into the sender, and defer slow work to a
  Celery task via `transaction.on_commit`.
- Secrets come from `.env` via `decouple.config` — never hardcoded, and every new key is
  added to `.env.example` too.
- Tests run on Postgres, never SQLite.
- Anything new in `core/` gets a test in `core/tests/`.

