## Definition of done

Run `make check`, then walk `docs/INTEGRATION-GUIDE.md` §9. Don't skip it because the
change looked small — that checklist exists because of the small ones. If an item can't
be satisfied, **say so explicitly** rather than marking it done on an assumption.

## When something doesn't fit cleanly

If a piece of new logic could plausibly be reused in another project, **say so before
writing it into `core/`.** `core/` is the right home for glue that's specific to this
project; a self-contained capability probably wants to be a new app package instead
(`docs/APP-DESIGN.md`). Defaulting to `core/` because it's the path of least resistance is
how this architecture's reuse benefit quietly erodes.

