# CLAUDE.md — {{APP_NAME}} (app package)

A standalone, versioned, dual-package Django + React app package. It is installed into host
projects as read-only third-party code and must work in **any** host.

**Read `docs/APP-DESIGN.md` in full before making changes.** This file is the fast reference.

## The rules that define this package

1. **Never import another app package.** Not in code, not in `pyproject.toml`. The only
   sanctioned cross-app reference is `settings.AUTH_USER_MODEL` (a string Django resolves at
   runtime). Anything else is the host's job, in its `core/`. → `APP-DESIGN.md` §6
2. **Never import anything host-specific** — no `tools.*`, no `core.*`, no assumption about
   the host's folder layout. Bundle an internal equivalent in `utils.py`. → §4
3. **Public surface is exactly three things:** `signals.py` (events), `services.py`
   (callables), `factories.py` (test-only). Models, views, and serializers are internal.
   The frontend's public surface is exactly `src/index.ts` — the manager is never exported.
4. **Wide dependency ranges, never exact pins**, on anything a host also uses
   (`django`, `djangorestframework`, `celery`, …). Every installed app resolves into one
   shared environment, so an exact pin makes this package un-combinable. → §1.1
5. **Both halves release under one tag.** `backend/pyproject.toml`, `frontend/package.json`,
   and `CHANGELOG.md` must state the same version — CI fails the build otherwise. → §11
6. **Namespace everything that lands in a shared namespace** — throttle scopes, settings
   keys, `.env` keys, query keys, cache keys, task names all carry the app's name. → §1.3

## Commands

```bash
cd backend && uv sync             # dev + test groups included
uv run pytest                     # authoritative gate for the Python half
uv run ruff check --fix . && uv run ruff format .
uv run mypy src
uv build                          # what CI's wheel-smoke-test builds

cd frontend && npm ci
npm run test                      # Vitest + MSW — authoritative gate for the TS half
npx tsc --noEmit && npm run lint

# Verify the two halves against a real host before tagging — the highest-value check
cd playground/backend && uv sync
docker compose -f playground/docker-compose.yml up
```

## Semver triggers — these are MAJOR bumps even when the diff is small

- Removing or renaming a **signal kwarg**, or renaming a signal.
- Changing a **`services.py` method signature**.
- Renaming or removing a **factory**.
- Removing an export from `src/index.ts`, or changing a hook's return shape.
- Renaming a settings key, `.env` key, or throttle scope (host config breaks silently).

Anything above needs a **Host action:** line in `CHANGELOG.md` saying what a host must change.

## Definition of done

- `README.md`'s copy-paste config block matches reality: settings, `.env` keys, throttle
  scopes, URL mounts, signal payload table, service signatures, factories, exported hooks.
  → `APP-DESIGN.md` §8
- Security checklist walked, not assumed — including an IDOR test per endpoint. → §9
- Every service has a happy + failure path test; every view has 200/403/401; every hook has
  a success + error test; every emitted signal is asserted with its exact payload. → §7.4
- Version bumped in all three places; `CHANGELOG.md` entry written. → §11
- Playground verified. CI green, including `resolution-matrix` and `wheel-smoke-test`.
- App registry entry updated with the new version. → `BASE-DESIGN.md` §11.3
